---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import Showcase from "../../../components/Showcase.astro";
import StylingHooks from "../../../components/StylingHooks.astro";

const install = `pnpm add @skryensya/core @skryensya/vanilla`;

const styles = `@import "@skryensya/core/patterns/anchored.css";
@import "@skryensya/core/components/select.css";`;

const nativeInstall = `pnpm add @skryensya/core`;

const selectHtml = `<div
  class="sk-select"
  data-sk-select
  id="plan"
  data-value="starter"
>
  <label class="sk-select__label" data-sk-select-label>
    Plan
  </label>

  <button
    class="sk-select__trigger sk-anchor sk-interactive"
    data-sk-select-trigger
    type="button"
  >
    <span class="sk-select__value" data-sk-select-value>
      Starter
    </span>
    <span
      class="sk-select__indicator"
      data-sk-select-indicator
      aria-hidden="true"
    >
      <span data-state="closed">
        <span data-sk-icon="chevron-down"></span>
      </span>
      <span data-state="open">
        <span data-sk-icon="chevron-up"></span>
      </span>
    </span>
  </button>

  <div
    class="sk-select__positioner sk-anchored"
    data-sk-select-positioner
  >
    <ul class="sk-select__content" data-sk-select-content>
      <li
        class="sk-select__item sk-interactive"
        data-sk-select-item
        data-value="starter"
      >
        <span
          class="sk-select__item-text"
          data-sk-select-item-text
        >
          Starter
        </span>
        <span
          class="sk-select__item-indicator"
          data-sk-select-item-indicator
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <span data-sk-icon="check"></span>
        </span>
      </li>
      <li
        class="sk-select__item sk-interactive"
        data-sk-select-item
        data-value="pro"
      >
        <span
          class="sk-select__item-text"
          data-sk-select-item-text
        >
          Pro
        </span>
        <span
          class="sk-select__item-indicator"
          data-sk-select-item-indicator
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <span data-sk-icon="check"></span>
        </span>
      </li>
      <li
        class="sk-select__item sk-interactive"
        data-sk-select-item
        data-value="enterprise"
      >
        <span
          class="sk-select__item-text"
          data-sk-select-item-text
        >
          Enterprise
        </span>
        <span
          class="sk-select__item-indicator"
          data-sk-select-item-indicator
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <span data-sk-icon="check"></span>
        </span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>`;

const js = `import { initComponents } from "@skryensya/vanilla/auto";
import { mountIcons } from "@skryensya/vanilla/icon";
import { lucideIcons } from "@skryensya/icons-lucide";

// Icons are authored as <span data-sk-icon> placeholders;
// mountIcons replaces them with the <svg> of the linked set.
mountIcons(document, lucideIcons);

await initComponents();`;

const listen = `document
  .getElementById("plan")
  .addEventListener("sk-value-change", (event) => {
    console.log(event.detail.value); // ["pro"]
  });`;

const forms = `<div
  class="sk-select"
  data-sk-select
  id="plan"
>
  <!-- Optional: causes the Select to be sent in a form, and is what
       which is left without JS. Your <option> have to match
       the items, or the enhancer strips. -->
  <select data-sk-select-hidden name="plan">
    <option value="starter">Starter</option>
    <option value="pro">Pro</option>
  </select>
  …
</div>`;

const reactSelect = `import { Icon } from "@skryensya/react/icon";
import { Select } from "@skryensya/react/select";

<Select
  label="Plan"
  name="plan"
  defaultValue={["starter"]}
  indicator={<Icon name="chevron-down" />}
  openIndicator={<Icon name="chevron-up" />}
  itemIndicator={<Icon name="check" />}
  options={[
    { value: "starter", label: "Starter" },
    { value: "pro", label: "Pro" },
    { value: "enterprise", label: "Enterprise" },
  ]}
/>;`;

const nativeSelectHtml = `<div class="sk-stack" data-gap="xs">
  <label for="native-plan">Plan</label>
  <select class="sk-select-native" id="native-plan" name="plan">
    <option value="starter">Starter</option>
    <option value="pro">Pro</option>
    <option value="enterprise">Enterprise</option>
  </select>
</div>`;

const nativeReactSelect = `import { NativeSelect } from "@skryensya/react/select-native";

<NativeSelect
  aria-label="Plan"
  name="plan"
  options={[
    { value: "starter", label: "Starter" },
    { value: "pro", label: "Pro" },
  ]}
/>;`;
---

<Base
  title="Select"
  description="Select: A machine-enhanced listbox, for Vanilla and React."
>
  <h1>Select</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The main selector when the interaction needs typeahead, highlight, controlled popup and
    positioning. <code>Select</code> shares his parts contract on
    <code>@skryensya/vanilla</code> and <code>@skryensya/react</code>; the machine of each binding is a
    internal detail.
  </p>

  <p>
    For a standard choice of form, use the
    <a href="#select-nativo">Select native</a> documented at the end: does not load an enhancer, keeps
    platform behavior and stylizes your picker through progressive improvement.
  </p>

  <Showcase html={selectHtml} react={reactSelect} label="Select enhanced" viewport="menu" />
  <p>
    Density compacts the space around the selector, not its tactile objectives: the trigger and
    each option retains a minimum of <code>44px</code> height.
  </p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={install} label="terminal" />
  <CodeBlock code={styles} label="CSS" lang="css" />

  <h2>HTML autorado</h2>
  <p>
    The items <strong>are</strong> the collection: the enhancer reads them from the DOM, just like tabs reads their
    triggers. Each <code>data-sk-select-item</code> needs a <code>data-value</code>. The markup
    The full version is in the <strong>Vanilla</strong> tab of the preview.
  </p>

  <h2>Initialize Vanilla</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={js} label="JavaScript" />

  <h2>Hear the change</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={listen} label="JavaScript" />

  <h2>Forms and fallback without JavaScript</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={forms} label="HTML" />

  <h2>Contrato enhanced</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The root carries <code>data-sk-select</code> and the parts anatomy documented.</li>
    <li>The enhancer does not render markup or invent classes; only connects authored nodes.</li>
    <li>The text of the value is owned by the machine; placeholder, options and ids remain the consumer's.</li>
    <li>React renders the same contract and does not hydrate the vanilla markup.</li>
  </ul>

  <StylingHooks groups={[
      { file: "components/select.css", probe: "sk-select" },
      { file: "patterns/anchored.css", probe: "sk-anchored", title: "Anchor Inherits" },
    ]} />

  <h2>Select nativo</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    It is a real <code>&lt;select&gt;</code>: the selection, the keyboard, the form submission and the
    Accessibility still belongs to the browser. Allison applies
    <code>sk-select-native</code>; there is no <code>data-sk-*</code>, machine or package
    <code>@skryensya/vanilla</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Use it for a standard choice. Choose Select enhanced only when you need your collection
    controlled, item markup, positioning or event <code>sk-value-change</code>; the appearance
    no longer a reason to replace the native control.
  </p>
  <Showcase html={nativeSelectHtml} react={nativeReactSelect} label="Select nativo" viewport="menu" />

  <h3>Mejora progresiva</h3>
  <p>
    If the browser supports <code>appearance: base-select</code> and
    <code>::picker(select)</code>, Core applies the same to the field, the picker and its options
    surface, spacing, states and icons that Select uses. Other browsers ignore that block
    and they preserve the classic popup of the operating system. The HTML and behavior do not change.
  </p>

  <h3>Install only the native Select</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={nativeInstall} label="terminal" />
  <CodeBlock code={styles} label="CSS" lang="css" />

  <h3>Contrato nativo</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Use an associated <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> or equivalent accessible name.</li>
    <li>The selection, keyboard, and serialization of <code>form</code> belong to the browser.</li>
    <li><code>disabled</code> is the native attribute; It is not replaced by JavaScript state.</li>
    <li>Customizable select makes the picker uniform; the classic popup is still the fallback.</li>
  </ul>

  <StylingHooks groups={[{ file: "components/select.css", probe: "sk-select-native" }]} />
</Base>
